# THE ORDERING CONTROL for the include-path fallback.
#
# Compiled with `-Itest/ffi_headers/`, which also has a `sub/marker.h` -- with a
# different value. This program sits next to its own, so its own must win. If the
# fallback ever ran FIRST, this row prints 4242 and nothing else in the suite
# would notice: both headers resolve, both compile, and the wrong constant is a
# plausible number.
import "sub/marker.h"
print(FFI_MARKER)
